## 2. Naming Conventions

### ✅ Followed
- `*UseCase` for inbound ports (`GetInvestorPortfolioUseCase`, `ConvertToMobilePortfolioUseCase`).
- `*Port` for outbound ports (`LoadInvestorPort`, `LoadCamsFolioMasterPort`).
- `*Service` implementing the matching `*UseCase`.
- `*PersistenceAdapter` implementing a `Load*Port`.
- `*Mapper` for transformation classes (`PersistenceMapper`, `CapitalGainReportMapper`, `MobilePortfolioMapper`).

### ❌ Not followed
- No `*Request`/`*Response` DTO naming — API layer returns domain models directly.
- Domain/entity field names use snake_case (`type_id`, `client_name`, `is_purchase_allowed`) instead of Java camelCase — deliberate per README (DB column fidelity), but a deviation from normal Java and from the reference's convention table.
- Mixed snake_case/camelCase `@RequestParam` names in the same controller (e.g. `financial_year` alongside camelCase params).

### 🔧 Needs attention
- If snake_case fields are intentional (legacy fidelity), document this explicitly as an approved exception in this repo's own coding guidelines doc (see §7) so it doesn't get "fixed" inconsistently later.

