## 4. Unit Test Coverage

### ✅ Followed
- Correct framework stack: JUnit 5 + Mockito + AssertJ + `MockMvc` (standalone setup) — matches the reference stack.
- Test naming and style are good where present: `InvestorPortfolioControllerTest` uses `@Nested`, `@DisplayName`, `@ParameterizedTest`, mirrors the reference's readability conventions.

### ❌ Not followed — critical gap
Only **2 test files exist for 108 main classes**:
- `InvestorPortfolioControllerTest` (good coverage of the controller)
- `MfboxUtilsTest` (covers one utility class)

**Entirely untested** (no test file at all):
- `InvestorPortfolioService` (3,453 lines) — the largest and most business-critical class in the service
- `InvestorTaxReportService` (1,286 lines)
- `FamilyMfPortfolioService` (374 lines)
- `FolioMasterSummaryService` (289 lines)
- `CapitalGainReportMapper` (455 lines), `MobilePortfolioMapper` (265 lines)
- All 13 classes in `adapter/out/persistence/*PersistenceAdapter`
- `PersistenceMapper` (generic reflective `BeanUtils` mapper — failure modes untested)
- `XIRR` (256-line numerical solver — exactly the kind of code that most needs edge-case unit tests: convergence failure, negative cash flows, single transaction, etc.)
- `MyMFBoxUtils`, `TrackerUtils`, `TransactionDataUtils`

No JaCoCo (or any) coverage gate is configured, so this gap won't show up as a build failure — it will only show up as a production incident.

### 🔧 Needs attention — this is the single biggest risk in the codebase
- Prioritize unit tests for `InvestorPortfolioService`, `InvestorTaxReportService`, and `XIRR` first — highest line count and highest financial-calculation risk.
- Add persistence adapter tests (even simple Mockito-based ones, or `@DataJpaTest` if a test DB is available).
- Configure a JaCoCo coverage floor on `application` and `domain` packages, matching the reference's 80% instruction-coverage gate.
- The README's claim of being "diffed against original" is a manual/textual check, not automated test coverage — do not treat it as equivalent to unit tests.

