## What You Should NOT Do

- **Do not** add more business logic to `InvestorPortfolioService` or `InvestorTaxReportService` before adding tests — the class is already 3,453 lines with zero coverage; growing it further compounds the risk.
- **Do not** deploy `application-prod.properties` as-is — the port collision with the legacy service and the plaintext secrets make this unsafe to run in a shared environment.
- **Do not** treat the "diffed against original" note in the README as equivalent to automated test coverage when deciding this service is production-ready — it is not.
- **Do not** copy the field-injection pattern in `application/service/*` or the inconsistent try/catch pattern in `InvestorPortfolioController` into new services — these are the two coding-guideline deviations most likely to spread if this becomes the next template.
- **Do not** silently "fix" the snake_case field names or the direct domain-as-response pattern without team agreement — both appear to be deliberate tradeoffs (legacy fidelity, avoiding a 200-field remap), not oversights. Confirm before changing.
- **Do not** reuse this repository as a new team template until at minimum: constructor injection is applied uniformly, a global exception handler exists, secrets are externalized, and the core business-logic classes have unit tests. Copying it today would propagate all of the above gaps to every future service.

